        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "7fc08271-05d6-5158-b276-6b55904f00cd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Hilda Neihardt, John G. Neihardt, Black Elk\n- Works: Black Elk Speaks\n- Roles: official observer, Oglala Lakota medicine man, Lakota holy man\n\nFacts:\n- In 1932, John G. Neihardt published Black Elk Speaks, a book that relates the story of Black Elk.\n- Black Elk was an Oglala Lakota medicine man and Lakota holy man.\n- At age 15, Hilda Neihardt accompanied her father John G. Neihardt as an official observer to meetings with Black Elk.\n- Hilda Neihardt was one of John G. Neihardt's \"comrades in adventure.\"\n- The life stories Black Elk shared with John G. Neihardt were the basis for Black Elk Speaks and for Hilda Neihardt's later works.\n- Hilda Neihardt lived from 1916 to 2004.",
